      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Byte-Level BPE & The Vocabulary File (Concepts 3 & 4)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Byte-Level BPE & The Vocabulary File (Concepts 3 & 4)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c75929b5-9fc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 245,
      "width": 520.8,
      "height": 275.40000000000003,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#083344",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 6985,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is Byte-Level BPE (Byte Pair Encoding)?\n\u2022 LLMs process subword chunks, NOT raw characters or full words.\n\u2022 Starts with 256 raw bytes and iteratively merges frequent pairs.\n\u2022 Byte-level guarantees ZERO 'unknown token' (<unk>) errors:\n  any Unicode, emoji, or symbol falls back to raw byte tokens.\n\nThe '\u0120' Leading-Space Quirk (GPT-2 / Qwen Byte Mapping):\n\u2022 Byte-level BPE maps all 256 bytes to printable Unicode chars.\n\u2022 Space (0x20) maps to '\u0120' (U+0120). Example:\n  ' sum' -> '\u0120sum' (Token ID 1242)  !=  'sum' (no leading space)\n\u2022 If you compare raw vocab strings without byte-decoding, space\n  and newline checks fail silently!\n\nInverting vocab.json (get_path_to_vocab_file()):\n\u2022 vocab.json maps:  token_string -> token_id (~151,936 entries)\n\u2022 Invert once at startup: id_to_str = {v: k for k, v in vocab.items()}\n\u2022 Gives O(1) lookup: 'If model picks ID X, what chars are added?'",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is Byte-Level BPE (Byte Pair Encoding)?\n\u2022 LLMs process subword chunks, NOT raw characters or full words.\n\u2022 Starts with 256 raw bytes and iteratively merges frequent pairs.\n\u2022 Byte-level guarantees ZERO 'unknown token' (<unk>) errors:\n  any Unicode, emoji, or symbol falls back to raw byte tokens.\n\nThe '\u0120' Leading-Space Quirk (GPT-2 / Qwen Byte Mapping):\n\u2022 Byte-level BPE maps all 256 bytes to printable Unicode chars.\n\u2022 Space (0x20) maps to '\u0120' (U+0120). Example:\n  ' sum' -> '\u0120sum' (Token ID 1242)  !=  'sum' (no leading space)\n\u2022 If you compare raw vocab strings without byte-decoding, space\n  and newline checks fail silently!\n\nInverting vocab.json (get_path_to_vocab_file()):\n\u2022 vocab.json maps:  token_string -> token_id (~151,936 entries)\n\u2022 Invert once at startup: id_to_str = {v: k for k, v in vocab.items()}\n\u2022 Gives O(1) lookup: 'If model picks ID X, what chars are added?'",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
