      "text": "2. Logits, Softmax & Greedy Decoding (Concept 1)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. Logits, Softmax & Greedy Decoding (Concept 1)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2a946cc6-ac4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 670,
      "y": 245,
      "width": 513.36,
      "height": 275.40000000000003,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 47611,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is a Logit?\n\u2022 Given context x_{1..t}, the LLM outputs a vector z in R^|V|\n  (~151,936 raw, unnormalized real scores: negative, zero, positive).\n\u2022 Higher logit z_i = higher model confidence for token i.\n\nSoftmax Probability Conversion:\n  P(token_i | context) = exp(z_i) / sum_j( exp(z_j) )\n\nWhy Set Illegal Logits to -math.inf (-\u221e)?\n\u2022 exp(-\u221e) = 0  =>  P(illegal_token) = 0.0 (exact zero!).\n\u2022 A finite penalty (e.g., -100) could still win if all legal tokens\n  had even lower logits (-200). -\u221e makes selection impossible.\n\nGreedy Argmax Decoding:\n\u2022 Because exp(z) is strictly monotonic, argmax(P) == argmax(z).\n\u2022 We skip Softmax completely and pick: next_id = argmax(masked_z).\n\u2022 Deterministic & reproducible (temperature = 0, no sampling).",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is a Logit?\n\u2022 Given context x_{1..t}, the LLM outputs a vector z in R^|V|\n  (~151,936 raw, unnormalized real scores: negative, zero, positive).\n\u2022 Higher logit z_i = higher model confidence for token i.\n\nSoftmax Probability Conversion:\n  P(token_i | context) = exp(z_i) / sum_j( exp(z_j) )\n\nWhy Set Illegal Logits to -math.inf (-\u221e)?\n\u2022 exp(-\u221e) = 0  =>  P(illegal_token) = 0.0 (exact zero!).\n\u2022 A finite penalty (e.g., -100) could still win if all legal tokens\n  had even lower logits (-200). -\u221e makes selection impossible.\n\nGreedy Argmax Decoding:\n\u2022 Because exp(z) is strictly monotonic, argmax(P) == argmax(z).\n\u2022 We skip Softmax completely and pick: next_id = argmax(masked_z).\n\u2022 Deterministic & reproducible (temperature = 0, no sampling).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
