      "text": "3. Autoregressive Generation Loop (Concept 2)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Autoregressive Generation Loop (Concept 2)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1d5232ef-6fb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1310,
      "y": 245,
      "width": 483.6,
      "height": 243.00000000000003,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#3b0764",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 90656,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What does 'Autoregressive' Mean?\n\u2022 The model predicts ONE token at a time, conditioned on ALL\n  previously generated tokens: P(x_t | x_1, x_2, ..., x_{t-1}).\n\u2022 Each chosen token is appended to input_ids and fed back in.\n\nWhy the Loop is Your Control Point:\n\u2022 Because Python owns the loop between forward passes, we can:\n  1. INJECT known structural tokens directly (0 forward passes).\n  2. INTERCEPT logits at decision points and mask illegal IDs.\n\nBPE Context-Sensitivity & The 'Ratchet' (decode -> re-encode):\n\u2022 tokens('...foo') + tokens('bar') != tokens('...foobar') because\n  BPE merges depend on adjacent characters.\n\u2022 Re-encoding: working_ids = encode(decode(working_ids) + text)\n  keeps token boundaries 100% canonical so logits never degrade.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What does 'Autoregressive' Mean?\n\u2022 The model predicts ONE token at a time, conditioned on ALL\n  previously generated tokens: P(x_t | x_1, x_2, ..., x_{t-1}).\n\u2022 Each chosen token is appended to input_ids and fed back in.\n\nWhy the Loop is Your Control Point:\n\u2022 Because Python owns the loop between forward passes, we can:\n  1. INJECT known structural tokens directly (0 forward passes).\n  2. INTERCEPT logits at decision points and mask illegal IDs.\n\nBPE Context-Sensitivity & The 'Ratchet' (decode -> re-encode):\n\u2022 tokens('...foo') + tokens('bar') != tokens('...foobar') because\n  BPE merges depend on adjacent characters.\n\u2022 Re-encoding: working_ids = encode(decode(working_ids) + text)\n  keeps token boundaries 100% canonical so logits never degrade.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
