      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Validators as Finite-State Machines & Prefix Tries (Concept 6)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Validators as Finite-State Machines & Prefix Tries (Concept 6)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ddc1b227-801",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 670,
      "y": 705,
      "width": 840.72,
      "height": 226.8,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#451a03",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 53279,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Not a General JSON Parser? A full JSON parser allows ANY valid JSON, not our exact function-call schema.\nInstead, each value slot uses a dedicated, provably-correct miniature automaton:\n\n[A] PREFIX TRIE (function_name.py)                      [B] ONE-SHOT BINARY STATE (boolean.py)\n    root -> 'fn' -> '_add' -> '_numbers' -> '\"'              States: {START} --(true_id | false_id)--> {END}\n                 -> '_greet' -> '\"'                          Single forward pass; compares 2 logits directly.\n    At each step, only tokens extending a valid prefix\n    stay unmasked. When a full name matches, '\"' unlocks.   [C] CHARACTER-CLASS FSM (number.py)\n                                                             Allowed: digits '0-9', '-', '.' | Stops: '}', ','\n[D] GUARDRAILED STRING AUTOMATON (string.py)                 Emits digit-by-digit until model picks a stop token.\n    \u2022 Hard Ban-List: '\"', '\\n', '\\r', curly quotes (close '\"' kept legal so string can always terminate).\n    \u2022 Soft Drift Terminators: '{', '}', '\\'', '.', '\\\\', '\\n', 'regex', 'replacement', 'source_string'.\n      If model selects a drift token after >=1 token, loop halts cleanly (prevents schema/JSON leakage).\n    \u2022 Cycle Detector (_would_repeat): halts if hypothetical[-p:] == hypothetical[-2p:-p] for p in 1..6.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Not a General JSON Parser? A full JSON parser allows ANY valid JSON, not our exact function-call schema.\nInstead, each value slot uses a dedicated, provably-correct miniature automaton:\n\n[A] PREFIX TRIE (function_name.py)                      [B] ONE-SHOT BINARY STATE (boolean.py)\n    root -> 'fn' -> '_add' -> '_numbers' -> '\"'              States: {START} --(true_id | false_id)--> {END}\n                 -> '_greet' -> '\"'                          Single forward pass; compares 2 logits directly.\n    At each step, only tokens extending a valid prefix\n    stay unmasked. When a full name matches, '\"' unlocks.   [C] CHARACTER-CLASS FSM (number.py)\n                                                             Allowed: digits '0-9', '-', '.' | Stops: '}', ','\n[D] GUARDRAILED STRING AUTOMATON (string.py)                 Emits digit-by-digit until model picks a stop token.\n    \u2022 Hard Ban-List: '\"', '\\n', '\\r', curly quotes (close '\"' kept legal so string can always terminate).\n    \u2022 Soft Drift Terminators: '{', '}', '\\'', '.', '\\\\', '\\n', 'regex', 'replacement', 'source_string'.\n      If model selects a drift token after >=1 token, loop halts cleanly (prevents schema/JSON leakage).\n    \u2022 Cycle Detector (_would_repeat): halts if hypothetical[-p:] == hypothetical[-2p:-p] for p in 1..6.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
